abstract: >-
  Lean 4 / Mathlib formalization of Monster Assignment Rigidity (MAR-1 to MAR-17).
  Main theorem (MAR-9): for the ATLAS data of the Monster, the Conway-Norton table
  is the only assignment of genus-zero labels n|h+W of Conway-Norton shape
  (385 candidates) that satisfies the Conway-Norton power rule, the vanishing of the
  first two McKay-Thompson coefficients forced by the label, and coherence of the
  first coefficient; each hypothesis is necessary (MAR-10). The same hypotheses do
  not determine the table for the Baby Monster or for Conway moonshine (MAR-11 to
  MAR-16). Every result is a Lean theorem with all computations checked by the
  kernel.
keywords:
  - monstrous moonshine
  - Monster group
  - Conway-Norton
  - Hauptmodul
